oes: comprise/1

# Khan Academy as a public sample Holotype, built only from public sources on 2026-10-18 (the nonprofit's own site and help pages, its Form 990 filings
# on ProPublica's Nonprofit Explorer, press pages and reputable reporting). Every node cites its sources; a fact that could not be confirmed
# from a current source is left pending. No person's name appears anywhere: roles and seats only, and the people file is never written.
# Layout: atoms/<slug>/<Module>/*.cosm. atom/khan-academy is modelled in all eight modules; atom/schoolhouse-world is thin (one entity and the mirrored
# bond). Khan Academy India and Brasil (controlled, per Form 990 Schedule R), Khan Lab School and Khan Schools Network (affiliated) are stubs in C.

id: holotype/khan-academy
name: Khan Academy
summary: "The nonprofit behind the free learning platform, its Khanmigo AI tutor, district partnerships, the Khan Academy Kids app and programs abroad, with its public financials by fiscal year; two atoms (itself and the separate nonprofit Schoolhouse World) joined by an affiliation bond, and four more related nonprofits as stubs."
sample: true
alignment:
  for: other
  mode: research
  by: "comprise-sample"
  at: 2026-10-18
atoms:
  - atom/khan-academy
  - atom/schoolhouse-world
perspective: atom/khan-academy

# Sources that nodes outside P cite are declared here; the sources P's own nodes cite are in atoms/khan-academy/P/doc.cosm.
sources:
